"frame_order":"","frame_interpolate":false,"visible":true,"internal":true,"saved":true,"uuid":"02c8f84c-0004-5b44-b2aa-2f375c5d73bf","relative_path":"dwarf_hall.png","source":"data:image/png;base64,"}],"animations":[],"description":"# dwarf_hall\n\nDwarf hall: a big dark stone hall on a stepped plinth, a pillared front of square columns with bronze capitals, a heavy flat roof with a stepped parapet.\n\n- Footprint: 14 x 10 columns (224 x 160 units, 6.30 x 4.50 m), centred on the origin, front (door side) faces -Z.\n- Finished bounds: x -104..104, y 0..152, z -84..76 units.\n- Texture: 512 x 512, 1 px per unit, square pixels, nearest filtering. Every visible face has its own texture region painted with its material at world position (seams line up across faces); identical faces share a region; construction and ruined pieces map into the region of the face they were cut from. No cube is cut to fit the texture.\n- Cubes: finished 74, construction_0 33, construction_33 53, construction_66 67, ruined 40 (2 rotated: roof slabs and a few leaning props).\n\n## Hit box\n\n- hall: 208 x 160 x 148 centred at x 0, z 2\n\n## State group sets (children of `root`; show exactly one)\n\n- `finished`: the finished building (visible by default).\n- `construction_0`, `construction_33`, `construction_66`: build progress at 0 %, 33 % and 66 % (staked outline and scaffold, then walls rising inside scaffold, then full frame with roof rafters).\n- `ruined`: collapsed shell, broken walls, rubble, fallen roof (use with `_damaged.png`, or `_abandoned.png` for F7 abandoned buildings).\n- `dwarf_hall_damaged.png`: damaged texture (scorch, holes, cracks) for the same UVs; works on every group set.\n- `dwarf_hall_abandoned.png`: abandoned look (damage plus moss, faded cloth, cold fires) = `abandoned_dwarf_hall` together with the `ruined` set or the finished set.\n\n## Attachment and effect points (empty groups)\n\n- `slot_door` at (0, 0, -92)\n"}